Roald Dahl claimed to have invented the word in a childrens' book called
"The Gremlins" in exactly this context (he was a WW2 fighter pilot; the
gremlins he described were imps who hung around in planes & made them crash).
The book is out of print, Disney began an animation of it which was never
finished. This claim is made in a short autobiography of his titled "Lucky
Break", published in a collection of seven short stories called "The Wonder-
ful Story of Henry Sugar".

